        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>IV:\r\n<style type=\"text/css\">\r\n<!--td {border: 1px solid #ccc;}br {mso-data-placement:same-cell;}--></style>\r\n<span style=\"font-size:110.0%;font-family:calibri,arial,sans,sans-serif;color:#000000;text-align:left;\">When this card enters play, destroy all other Distortion cards. Each Ongoing and Equipment card now has a maximum HP of 6.</span></p><p>LL:\r\n<style type=\"text/css\">\r\n<!--td {border: 1px solid #ccc;}br {mso-data-placement:same-cell;}--></style>\r\n<span style=\"font-size:110.0%;font-family:calibri,arial,sans,sans-serif;color:#000000;text-align:left;\">Whenever a Villain card would be destroyed, reveal the top card of the Villain deck. If it is not a Lucky card, discard it and prevent the card destruction. If it is a Lucky card, put it into play.</span></p><p>So, Kismet doesn&#39;t normally have targets in her deck, but IV can change that.&nbsp; What happens when the heroes reduce one of her Ongoings to &lt;=0 HP when LL is in play and you reveal a non-Lucky card?</p><p>I *think* that you &#39;prevent&#39; the destruction, but since it still has &lt;=0 HP, it is immediately destroyed again.&nbsp; So, basically, you&#39;d keep revealing and discarding non-Lucky cards until you got a Lucky one.&nbsp;</p><p>Thoughts?</p>",
